    "result_text": "All 33 tests pass with `BUILD SUCCESS`. The change is complete.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `bulkSignupWarning` flag on owner creation. When more than 80 owners have already been created for the new owner's registration business day, the response now includes `\"bulkSignupWarning\": true`; otherwise `false`.\n\nFollowing this project's OfficeFloor function-injection conventions and the existing `namesakeCount` precedent (a create-time snapshot persisted on the owner and surfaced through the DTO), the change spans:\n\n- **New step** `AssignBulkSignupWarning.java` \u2014 counts existing owners already persisted against the resolved registration business day and stamps `owner.setBulkSignupWarning(count > 80)`. It runs after `BuildOwner`/`AssignNamesakeCount` and before `SaveOwner`, so the count excludes the owner being created and reuses the same accumulation path as the daily-limit rule.\n- **Pipeline wiring** in `owners.POST.yml` \u2014 inserted `flagBulkSignup` between `countNamesakes` and `save`, under the same `transaction` governance.\n- **`Owner` model** \u2014 added the `bulkSignupWarning` (`Boolean`) field with `@Column(name = \"bulk_signup_warning\")` plus getter/setter. MapStruct maps it to `OwnerDto` by name automatically.\n- **OpenAPI spec** (`openapi.yml`) \u2014 added the read-only `bulkSignupWarning` boolean property to the `Owner` schema so the generated `OwnerDto` carries it.\n- **Schema DDL** \u2014 added the `bulk_signup_warning` column to all four dialects (hsqldb, h2, mysql, postgres); the test profile uses hsqldb with `ddl-auto=none`, so the column must be declared explicitly.\n\nThe new `Cp22Tests` (fresh create \u2192 GET \u2192 `bulkSignupWarning` is `false`) passes, and all 33 tests remain green.",
